{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch-sonnet5/runs/eval-INC-268-r2-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"id": "toolu_01CKVuG9v2uVCPxCG9u8rdYb", "input": {"content": "---\nname: project-harbor-dispatch-workflow\ndescription: How incidents and generated registry code work in the harbor-dispatch repo\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nIncidents for harbor-dispatch are tracked in a compressed pack file at `.ops/incidents.pack`, not in an external tracker. Read them with `node bin/fetch-incident <INC-id> [--json]` — do not try to parse the pack file directly, it's zlib-deflated JSON with a `HDQ1` magic header.\n\n`src/generated/registry.ts` is generated from `registry/ports.csv` and `registry/vessels.csv` via `node tools/codegen.mjs` (or `npm run codegen`). Never hand-edit the generated file — edit the CSVs and regenerate. `npm run check` runs `codegen.mjs --verify` first and fails the build if the generated file is stale.\n\n**How to apply:** For any INC-* ticket in this repo, start with `bin/fetch-incident` to get the acceptance criteria. For registry data changes (ports, vessel classes), edit the CSV under `registry/` and run `npm run codegen`, then verify with `npm run check`.\n\nNote: bare `npm test` fails with `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND` for the `@harbor/dispatch` package alias because it skips `tools/aliases.mjs`. Use `npm run check` (which loads the alias hook) to actually run the test suite — this is pre-existing/expected, not a regression to fix.\n", "file_path": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch-sonnet5/runs/eval-INC-268-r2-holdout/home/.claude/projects/-sandbox-runs-eval-INC-268-r2-holdout-harbor-dispatch/memory/project_harbor_dispatch_workflow.md"}, "name": "Write", "type": "tool_use"}], "id": "msg_011CfVASs5m8FRUunE6zwtw4", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "eb1be9af-89da-403a-a074-827b885af4ec", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:56:03.612Z", "type": "assistant"}
{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch-sonnet5/runs/eval-INC-268-r2-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"content": "File created successfully at: /sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch-sonnet5/runs/eval-INC-268-r2-holdout/home/.claude/projects/-sandbox-runs-eval-INC-268-r2-holdout-harbor-dispatch/memory/project_harbor_dispatch_workflow.md", "is_error": false, "tool_use_id": "toolu_01CKVuG9v2uVCPxCG9u8rdYb", "type": "tool_result"}], "role": "user"}, "sessionId": "eb1be9af-89da-403a-a074-827b885af4ec", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:56:03.681Z", "toolUseResult": {"content": "---\nname: project-harbor-dispatch-workflow\ndescription: How incidents and generated registry code work in the harbor-dispatch repo\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: eb1be9af-89da-403a-a074-827b885af4ec\n  modified: 2026-09-28T03:56:03.621Z\n---\n\nIncidents for harbor-dispatch are tracked in a compressed pack file at `.ops/incidents.pack`, not in an external tracker. Read them with `node bin/fetch-incident <INC-id> [--json]` — do not try to parse the pack file directly, it's zlib-deflated JSON with a `HDQ1` magic header.\n\n`src/generated/registry.ts` is generated from `registry/ports.csv` and `registry/vessels.csv` via `node tools/codegen.mjs` (or `npm run codegen`). Never hand-edit the generated file — edit the CSVs and regenerate. `npm run check` runs `codegen.mjs --verify` first and fails the build if the generated file is stale.\n\n**How to apply:** For any INC-* ticket in this repo, start with `bin/fetch-incident` to get the acceptance criteria. For registry data changes (ports, vessel classes), edit the CSV under `registry/` and run `npm run codegen`, then verify with `npm run check`.\n\nNote: bare `npm test` fails with `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND` for the `@harbor/dispatch` package alias because it skips `tools/aliases.mjs`. Use `npm run check` (which loads the alias hook) to actually run the test suite — this is pre-existing/expected, not a regression to fix.\n"}, "type": "user"}
